# UtilityScope APAC

Daily intelligence platform for Asia-Pacific power markets.

## Site structure

```
utilityscope/
├── index.html              ← Homepage / dashboard
├── css/style.css           ← All styles (shared)
├── js/nav.js               ← Shared nav + footer
├── data/markets.json       ← ALL DATA LIVES HERE — edit this weekly
├── pages/
│   ├── markets.html        ← Markets overview
│   ├── utilities.html      ← Utility directory
│   ├── events.html         ← Event feed
│   ├── newsletter.html     ← Signup page
│   ├── about.html          ← About + methodology
│   └── methodology.html    ← (same as about)
├── markets/
│   ├── japan.html          ← Full Japan market page
│   ├── australia.html      ← Stub (expand later)
│   ├── singapore.html      ← Stub (expand later)
│   ├── korea.html          ← Stub (expand later)
│   └── taiwan.html         ← Stub (expand later)
└── utilities/
    └── tepco.html          ← TEPCO profile (expand for others)
```

## Updating data (your weekly task — no coding required)

Open `data/markets.json` in any text editor and update:

1. **prices** — change the `"price"` field for each market
2. **change** — update the % change (use minus sign for down: "-1.2")
3. **status** — "normal", "elevated", or "alert"
4. **demand** — the percentage (number only, e.g. 71)
5. **demandStatus** — "Normal", "Elevated", or "Grid Alert"
6. **events** — add new events at the top of the events array
7. **lastUpdated** — change the date/time string

Save the file. Redeploy (or if Vercel is connected to GitHub, just commit and push).

## Deploying to Vercel (one-time setup)

1. Create a free account at vercel.com
2. Click "Add New Project"
3. Import from GitHub (upload this folder to a GitHub repo first)
4. Vercel auto-detects static site — click Deploy
5. Your site is live at yourname.vercel.app
6. Add custom domain in Vercel Settings → Domains

Every time you update `data/markets.json` and push to GitHub, Vercel redeploys automatically in ~30 seconds.

## Connecting Mailchimp

1. Create free Mailchimp account
2. Create an Audience (email list)
3. Go to Embedded Forms → generate signup form code
4. Replace the form in `pages/newsletter.html` with your Mailchimp embed code

## Adding a new event

In `data/markets.json`, add to the top of the `"events"` array:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "severity": "high",
  "market": "Japan",
  "title": "Your event title here",
  "summary": "A sentence or two explaining what happened and why it matters.",
  "time": "08:45",
  "date": "6 Jun 2026"
}
```

Severity options: "high", "medium", "low"

